This license governs the successor release tseZharfaKavosh
v0.1.0.0 and the project material authorized for that release by
the rights holder. The project preserves the attribution and
lineage of the upstream projects identified above.

Historical upstream artifacts retain their original notices and
lineage, including the inherited Smart-FFA-1.0 notice where it
was issued. This successor notice does not erase, misrepresent,
or retroactively rewrite those historical notices.


PREAMBLE
--------

This license grants freedom to use, study, modify, and
redistribute this software. It requires attribution to the
original author. It permits, but does not require, optional
donation to support continued development.

The license is designed for projects that value both freedom
and sustainability. Attribution is mandatory. Donation is not.


PERMISSIONS
----------

You are free to:

  - Use this software for any purpose, commercial or
    non-commercial.
  - Study the source code and understand how it works.
  - Modify the source code to suit your needs.
  - Redistribute the original or modified software.
  - Fork the software and create derivative works.
  - Sublicense the software under the same terms.
  - Bundle this software with other software.
  - Sell services based on this software.


CONDITIONS
----------

When you fork, redistribute, or create a derivative work, you
must:

  1. Preserve the original author's name and address in the
     header of every source file that derives from this
     software.

  2. Preserve the Smart-FFA license identification in the
     header of every source file.

  3. Preserve the fork/upstream lineage explicitly. A fork
     must clearly state which project it is derived from.

  4. Not remove, obscure, replace, or misrepresent the
     upstream attribution.

  5. Not present upstream donation channels as if they belong
     to your own fork.

  6. Not condition any feature of your fork or derivative on
     receipt of donation.

  7. Not track, store, or share information about who has or
     has not donated.

You may:

  - Add your own author name and version details alongside
    the upstream attribution.
  - Add your own donation channels.
  - Remove upstream donation channels from your fork.
  - Combine upstream channels with your own, provided it is
    clear which channel belongs to which maintainer.


OPTIONAL DONATION
-----------------

This project may accept optional donations from users who wish
to support its continued development.

Donation is:

  - Voluntary. Never required.
  - Not a license fee.
  - Not a subscription.
  - Not a condition of use.
  - Not a condition of forking.
  - Not a condition of redistribution.
  - Not a feature unlock.
  - Not a royalty.
  - Not tracked by the project.

The project does not:

  - Track who has donated.
  - Store donation records.
  - Condition any feature on donation status.
  - Grant additional rights to donors.
  - Remove any obligation from donors.
  - Share donation information with third parties.

Donation records, if any, are held solely by the payment
processor chosen by the donor. The project does not have
access to donor identity beyond what the processor publicly
displays, unless the donor voluntarily shares it with the
project.


DONATION AND FORKS
------------------

A fork of this project may:

  a) Keep the upstream donation channels as-is.
  b) Remove the upstream donation channels entirely.
  c) Add its own donation channels.
  d) Combine upstream and own channels, provided the
     distinction is clear.

A fork must not:

  a) Remove upstream attribution to substitute its own
     donation channel.
  b) Present upstream donation channels as if they belong to
     the fork.
  c) Condition any feature on donation.
  d) Track donation status for any purpose that affects
     feature availability, access, or priority.


